[Term]
id: GO:0016507
name: mitochondrial fatty acid beta-oxidation multienzyme complex
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A multienzyme complex possessing three activities in two subunits (alpha and beta) that catalyzes three steps of the fatty acid beta-oxidation cycle within the mitochondrial matrix. The alpha subunit comprises the enoyl-CoA hydratase (ECH) and 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA dehydrogenase (HACD) activities, and the beta subunit contains the acetyl-CoA C-acyltransferase (KACT)/thiolase activity." [GOC:sjm, PMID:29915090]
