name: protein O-linked glycosylation via mannose
namespace: biological_process
def: "A glycoprotein biosynthetic process starting with the covalent linkage of a mannose via an alpha-glycosidic bond to the oxygen atom of a serine or threonine side chain in a protein, which can be further elongated with the sequential addition of sugar units resulting in the formation of a protein O-linked glycan." [PMID:35536928]
synonym: "protein amino acid O-linked mannosylation" EXACT [GOC:bf]
synonym: "protein O-linked mannosylation" RELATED []
