[Term]
id: GO:0071953
name: elastic fiber
namespace: cellular_component
def: "An supramolecular fiber that consists of an insoluble core of polymerized tropoelastin monomers and a surrounding mantle of microfibrils. Elastic fibers provide elasticity and recoiling to tissues and organs, and maintain structural integrity against mechanical strain." [GOC:BHF, PMID:12082143, PMID:16893474, PMID:20236620]
