[Term]
id: GO:0140507
name: granzyme-mediated programmed cell death signaling pathway
namespace: biological_process
def: "The series of molecular signals induced by granzymes which triggers the cell death of a cell. The pathway starts with reception of a granzyme signal, and ends when the execution phase of cell death is triggered. Granzymes are serine proteases that are secreted by cytotoxic T cells and natural killer cells to induce cell death in target cells." [PMID:32299851]
