[Term]
id: GO:0140680
name: histone H3K36me/H3K36me2 demethylase activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Catalysis of the removal of a methyl group from a di- or a monomethyl-lysine residue at position 36 of the histone H3 protein. This is a dioxygenase reaction that is dependent on Fe(II) and 2-oxoglutarate." [PMID:20531378]
comment: Comment: Note that the residue position corresponds to the canonical human H3 histone (UniProtKB:P84243); this residue is conserved across all eukaryotes. Residue 1 is the first residue following removal of the initiating Methionine (Met). Note that each histone is encoded by multiple genes, and sequences may vary across different genes within an organism.
synonym: "histone H3-di/monomethyl-lysine-36 demethylase activity" EXACT []
synonym: "histone H3K36me demethylase activity" RELATED []
synonym: "histone H3K36me2 demethylase activity" BROAD []
