[Term]
id: GO:7770030
name: rod photoreceptor phosphodiesterase 6 complex
namespace: cellular_component
def: "A heterotetrameric cGMP phosphodiesterase complex found in the disc membranes of rod photoreceptor outer segments. It consists of two catalytic subunits, PDE6A and PDE6B, and two inhibitory gamma-subunits, PDE6G. In response to activation by transducin, the complex hydrolyzes cyclic GMP, thereby mediating the light-induced closure of cGMP-gated ion channels during rod phototransduction." [PMID:38159849]
synonym: "rod PDE6 complex" EXACT []
synonym: "rod photoreceptor PDE6 complex" EXACT []
